Verse 32 & 33

If we confess Jesus as our Lord before men, Jesus will confess us to be worthy before God

If we deny Jesus, He will deny us before God in heaven





Reflections:

- Take aways for me from this chapter:

Jesus is telling his disciples to expect persecution for spreading the gospel

As Christians, it can be convenient to hide our faith in a sinful world to avoid people's judgement or persecution but that is not what jesus instructs us to to

To be a light for the world, we have to shine brightly. We have to be bold in our faith and not back down when the world tries to silence us

I'm not saying we necessarily need to overtly preach the gospel to every person we speak to, but I think Jesus would want to carry ourselves in the world as people who know truth and fear God which means we need not fear
judgement or perscution from men

Fear God and we don't need to fear anything else. Without the fear of God, there are many things to fear. 


Verse 38:


Most people living in the Roman Empire at this time would have had a vivid picture in mind of condemned criminals carrying the beam of their own cross toward the place of their execution. 

The Romans forced prisoners to do this as a kind of confession. By participating in their own execution, they were admitting—or, at least, submitting to the claim—that the Roman government was right to put them to death.

What could He possibly mean when He says that those who do not take up their cross and follow Him are not worthy of Him?

Jesus said to those who would follow Him that they must also participate in putting themselves to death. 

Seems like Jesus is that as believers we must die to ourselves.

We need to be willing to let go of our own agendas and personal dreams and ways of living. 

We must willingly submit to walking the difficult path of Christ all the way to the end of our lives. 

We can't call ourselves a follower of Jesus and, at the same time, follow our own path, do things our own way, ignore the righteous life God has called us to

If we don't die to ourselves and live for Jesus, we aren't worthy to follow Him.


That's a significant commitment. Something I will maritnate on for a while and hope you will too



